The public C header fixture in fixtures.hpp is copied as literal bytes from
DFDLSchemas/mil-std-2045, commit b1a489122f2d18bd3a329009d2a8c5f0ba0f0616,
src/test/resources/com/owlcyberdefense/mil-std-2045/milstd2045.tdml,
test_2045_C_msghdr1 and test_2045_C_msghdr1_unparsed. Upstream labels the
source K02.1_1.1.VMB modified to have zero message size. It is an envelope
fixture, not evidence of a valid empty K02.1 message or fielded traffic.

Other envelopes are synthetic verification data.
Payload examples are transcribed from MIL-STD-2045-47001C Table XIX and
MIL-STD-2045-47001D w/Change 1 Table B-II. See docs/format.md for the latter's
conflicting Field 2 character and published octet value.
